          "source": {"type":"pr","repo":"adobe/spectrum-design-data","number":1524,"title":"feat(design-data): promote public Spectrum Hub guidance to main","url":"https://github.com/adobe/spectrum-design-data/pull/1524"},
          "entries": [
            {"id":"ec3376fa-0","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/0","name":"guideline: Text overflow.\n\nWhen the tag text is too long fo","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Tags categorize content such as keywords or names. They’re often grouped to represent a search query or describe an item.","after":"Text overflow.\n\nWhen the tag text is too long for the available horizontal space or when a tag reaches its maximum width, it truncates. Hovering over the tag shows a tooltip with the full text."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-1","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/1","name":"guideline: RTL.\n\nFor RTL (right-to-left) languages, the lay","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Tags should always include a label. These can represent search terms, filters, or keywords.","after":"RTL.\n\nFor RTL (right-to-left) languages, the layout of the tag is mirrored. The avatar is right-aligned and the close button is left-aligned."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-2","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/2","name":"guideline: Keyboard interactions.\n\nKey Interaction Tab Tabb","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Tags have the option to include an avatar in addition to the label. These should be used to represent entities.","after":"Keyboard interactions.\n\nKey Interaction Tab Tabbing into a group of tags places the focus on the first tag (only one tag receives the keyboard focus at a time). Arrow keys Moves focus through the group of tags. Page Up or Page Down Moves focus to the previous or next tag in the group (last becomes first, and first becomes last). Home or End Moves focus to the first or last tag in the group. Backspace or Delete Removes the tag in focus from the group. Space If the tag is selectable, the space bar will toggle selection."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-3","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/3","name":"guideline: Cursor guidelines.\n\nCursor Description Default (","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Tags have the option to be removable or not. Removable tags have a small close (“x”) button.","after":"Cursor guidelines.\n\nCursor Description Default (Arrow) Use the default cursor for non-interactive tags. Pointer Use the pointer cursor for interactive tags, such as tags that are removable or can be used to filter content. Grab hand Use the grab hand cursor when the order of tags can be rearranged. Grab fist Use the grab fist cursor when holding a tag."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-4","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/4","name":"guideline: WCAG 2.2 compliance.\n\nAny criterion not mention ","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"A tag can be marked as having an error to show that it has become invalid.","after":"WCAG 2.2 compliance.\n\nAny criterion not mention in the below table are not applicable to this component or are resolved with underlying requirements, engineering, and styles of the entire system. 1. Perceivable Requirement Criterion Level Compliance Non-text content 1.1.1 A Non‑text elements—such as icons used in tags—must provide a text alternative that communicates the control’s purpose. All controls, especially icon‑only controls, need an accessible name (for example, via a title, aria‑label, or associated text) so screen readers can announce their function. Info and relationships, Identify purpose 1.3.1, 1.3.6 AA Tags should be understandable by assistive technologies like screen readers. This means the proper semantic HTML or ARIA role should be utilized. Text contrast 1.4.3 AA Large text has a contrast ratio of at least 3:1, and small text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1. Incidental text such as disabled, hidden, or decorative text has no contrast requirement. Resize text 1.4.4 AA Tags should be built in such a way that they can be resized without assistive technology up to 200%. Non-text contrast 1.4.11 AA The visual presentation of icons and various states have a contrast ratio of at least 3:1. Text spacing 1.4.12 AA Line height of text is at least 1.5x the font size. 2. Operable Requirement Criterion Level Compliance Keyboard 2.1.1, 2.1.3 A, AAA All functionality of the component is operable through a keyboard without specific timing for keystrokes. Keyboard traps 2.1.2 A Focus can be moved away from the component using only a keyboard. Seizures and physical reactions 2.3.1, 2.3.2, 2.3.3 A, AAA, AAA There is no flashing content or unnecessary motion or animation in this component. Focus order 2.4.3 A Navigation sequences receive focus in an order that preserves meaning and operability. Focus visible 2.4.7 AA Keyboard states use an indicator that is visible with at least 3:1 contrast."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-5","kind":"document-block","change":"removed","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/5","name":"guideline: A tag in a disabled state shows that a tag exist","fields":[],"before":{"type":"guideline","content":"A tag in a disabled state shows that a tag exists, but is not available in that circumstance. This can be used to maintain layout continuity and communicate that a tag may become available later."}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-6","kind":"document-block","change":"removed","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/6","name":"guideline: Tags have a read-only option for when content in","fields":[],"before":{"type":"guideline","content":"Tags have a read-only option for when content in the disabled state still needs to be shown. This allows for content to be copied, but not interacted with or changed."}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-7","kind":"document-block","change":"removed","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/7","name":"guideline: When the tag text is too long for the available ","fields":[],"before":{"type":"guideline","content":"When the tag text is too long for the available horizontal space or when a tag reaches its maximum width, it truncates. Hovering over the tag shows a tooltip with the full text."}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-8","kind":"document-block","change":"removed","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/8","name":"guideline: A tag can either trigger navigation or filtering","fields":[],"before":{"type":"guideline","content":"A tag can either trigger navigation or filtering, or act as a dismissible chip. Combining both interactions disrupts focus order and accessibility states. Choose one behavior — navigation or dismissal — and apply it consistently."}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-9","kind":"document-block","change":"added","class":"documentation","bump":"minor","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"tag/documentBlocks/9","name":"do-dont: Avoid conflicting tag actions","fields":[],"after":{"type":"do-dont","content":"Avoid conflicting tag actions","dont":"A tag can either trigger navigation or filtering, or act as a dismissible chip. Combining both interactions disrupts focus order and accessibility states. Choose one behavior — navigation or dismissal — and apply it consistently."}}
          ]
        }
      ]
